    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d952">

                <pb facs="0970" n="958" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg958"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/9183: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Yugoslavia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Belgrade</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-03-20T13:00:00+01:00">March 20, 1941—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 20—11:45 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>212. For the Secretary and Under Secretary. I learn the following indirectly from
                    the highest quarters: During German negotiations Yugoslavs put forward proposals
                    which they felt sure Germans would refuse. Yugoslavs now in embarrassing
                    position because Germans have accepted terms. Question up for decision by
                    Regency and Cabinet this morning. Yugoslavs will attempt delay signature of
                    pact, terms of which unknown to us, on ground that public opinion would <pb
                        facs="0971" n="959" xml:id="pg959"/> oppose it. British are arguing that
                    German acceptance of seemingly absurd terms is proof of German weakness and
                    should encourage Yugoslavs to refuse to sign. Croatian elements who favor
                    compromise with Germany oppose refusal to sign.</p>
                <p>Have reason to believe that Stojadinović<anchor n="56" xml:id="d952-f1"/> has
                    been secretly removed to Greece.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lane</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d952-f1" n="56" xml:id="d952-f1-content">
                <p>Milan Stojadinović, former Yugoslav Prime Minister.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
